&lt;p>Organizing multiple neurons into layers forms a neural network. The &amp;ldquo;deep&amp;rdquo; in deep learning refers to having many layers (typically more than 3).&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Large Language Models</title><link>https://martinsky999.github.io/en/ai-foundations/llm/</link><pubDate>Sun, 01 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://martinsky999.github.io/en/ai-foundations/llm/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="what-llms-really-are">What LLMs Really Are&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>A Large Language Model (LLM) is fundamentally a &lt;strong>next-token predictor&lt;/strong>: given a sequence of preceding tokens, predict the most likely next token.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>But when models become large enough (billions to trillions of parameters) and training data becomes vast enough (trillions of tokens), this simple objective produces emergent capabilities — reasoning, coding, translation, creative writing&amp;hellip;&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="transformer-the-foundation">Transformer: The Foundation&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>All major LLMs (GPT series, LLaMA, Claude, Gemini) are based on the Transformer architecture. Its core is &lt;strong>self-attention&lt;/strong>:&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Announcements</title><link>https://martinsky999.github.io/en/about/announcements/</link><pubDate>Wed, 01 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://martinsky999.github.io/en/about/announcements/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="announcements">Announcements&lt;/h2>
